To immerse the driver further, a digital twin of the city of Glasgow’s surrounding motorways has been modelled. The selected routes of M8, M73, and M80 formed a 28 miles triangle which is the busiest part of the road-network connecting Glasgow to Edinburgh and Stirling whilst offering the path to the north in Highlands and to the south towards North England as depicted in Figure 10 .
